      "text": "We set up a system of equations using the given points:\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= 4a + b, \\\\\n17 &= 8a + b.\n\\end{align*}Subtracting the first equation from the second gives: \\begin{align*}\n17 &= 8a + b \\\\\n- 5 &= 4a + b\\\\\n\\hline\n12 &= 4a\n\\end{align*}Solving for $a$, we find $4a = 12 \\implies a = 3$, so $3 + b = 5 \\implies b = -2$. Therefore, $a - b = 3 - (-2) = \\boxed{5}$.\n\nJust eliminate one of the equations with $b$ and solve for $a,$ then solve for $b$ and plug into the other equation to get the final answer.\nThe answer is: 5",
