      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We use $y=mx+c$ and seven given points, finding the values for $m$ and $c$ through the means of matrices.\n\nLet $\\left[\\begin{matrix} 4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ a \\\\ 5 \\end{matrix}\\right]$ be the first column of the matrix, \nand $\\left[\\begin{matrix} 8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ a \\\\ 17 \\end{matrix}\\right]$ be the second. \n\nThis can be written as $\\left[\\begin{matrix} 4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ a \\\\ 5 \\end{matrix}\\leftarrow \\left[\\begin{matrix} 8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ a \\\\ 17 \\end{matrix}\\right] \\rightarrow \\left[\\begin{matrix} 4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ a \\\\ 5 \\end{matrix}(\\cdot a) \\rightarrow 4a+1 \\end{equation}\\). \n\nThus, $5a+1=5$ and $8a+1=17$, so $a=1$. Then, $b=0$. So, $a-b=\\boxed{1}$.\n\nHere is the completed graph: [asy]\nunitsize (0.3 cm);\n\npair A, B, C;\n\nA = (0,0);\nB = (8,0);\nC = (44,4);\n\ndraw(A--B--C--A);\n\nlabel(\"$y$\", (9/2,0), N);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (0,9/2), E);\n\nlabel(\"$4$\", (2,0), N);\nlabel(\"$8$\", (6,0), N);\n[/asy] To solve the problem of finding the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) for the line \\(y = ax + b\\) given that it passes through the points \\((4, 5)\\) and \\((8, 17)\\), follow these steps:\n\n1. **Write the equations based on the given points:**\n   - When \\(x = 4\\), \\(y = 5\\), so \\(5 = 4a + b\\).\n   - When \\(x = 8\\), \\(y = 17\\), so \\(17 = 8a + b\\).\n\n2. **Set up a system of linear equations:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{cases} \n   5 = 4a + b \\\\\n   17 = 8a + b \n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Eliminate \\(b\\) by subtracting the first equation from the second:**\n   \\[\n   (17 = 8a + b) - (5 = 4a + b) \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b) \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 = 4a \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3 = a \n   \\]\n\n4. **Substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\(b\\). Using \\(5 = 4a + b\\) from our first equation:**\n   \\[\n   5 = 4(3) + b \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 = 12 + b \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = 5 - 12 \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   b = -7 \n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate \\(a - b\\):**\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7) \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 + 7 \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a - b = \\boxed{10}\n   \\]\n\nLet's now implement this process in Python with SymPy to verify our calculations.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\na, b = sp.symbols('a b')\n\n# Define the system of equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(4 * a + b, 5)\neq2 = sp.Eq(8 * a + b, 17)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2), (a, b))\n\n# Calculate a - b\na_value = solution[a]\nb_value = solution[b]\na_minus_b = a_value - b_value\n\nprint(a_minus_b)\n```",
